---
import Card from '@bdc/ui-astro/card/Card.astro';
import IconBadge from '@bdc/ui-astro/icon/IconBadge.astro';
import Hero from '@bdc/ui-astro/layout/Hero.astro';
import Link from '@bdc/ui-astro/link/Link.astro';
import InPageNav from '@components/layout/InPageNav.astro';
import NextStepsAlert from '@components/NextStepsAlert.astro';
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Researcher-Focused Initiatives">
  <Hero
    eyebrow="About BDC"
    titleLines={['Researcher-Focused', 'Initiatives']}
    description="See how BDC works with select research initiatives to bring valuable data and resources into the ecosystem and expand how researchers can use them."
  >
    <div slot="visual" class="width-full maxw-mobile-lg">
      <Card variant="panel">
        <div class="display-flex flex-align-center margin-bottom-1">
          <IconBadge icon="people" tone="secondary" size={6} iconSize={5} class="margin-right-105" />
        </div>
        <p class="font-sans-sm text-bold text-base-dark margin-top-1 ">More than hosting data</p>
        <p class="margin-top-2 margin-bottom-0 text-base line-height-sans-4">
          BDC works with research initiatives to make complex data more accessible, usable, and ready for analysis.
        </p>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </Hero>

  <section id="community-list" class="usa-section padding-top-4">
    <div class="grid-container">
      <InPageNav>
        <p>
          BDC collaborates with many of NHLBI's largest research communities by
          importing their data, integrating their resources (as appropriate), and
          providing analytical tools, applications, workflows, and secure
          workspaces.
        </p>
        <p>
          To support researchers from these communities when they start using the
          ecosystem, BDC develops and deploys enhancements, tailors the user
          onboarding process, and encourages participation in the greater BDC
          community. Researchers within these communities may use BDC to analyze
          scientific data collected from research protocols.
        </p>

        <div class="margin-bottom-8">
          <section id="topmed" class="border-top-1px border-base-light margin-top-6">
            <h2>TOPMed</h2>
            <p>
              TOPMed data in BDC combines whole-genome sequencing and other omics data 
              with rich clinical, behavioral, imaging, environmental, and molecular 
              data from studies spanning heart, lung, blood, and sleep research. BDC 
              provides secure access to these data alongside scalable analysis tools 
              and workflows, and hosts TOPMed Exchange Area (EA) data for TOPMed 
              investigators with approved access. <Link to="/help/contact-bdc">Contact 
              BDC</Link> if you are interested in accessing EA data in BDC.
            </p>
            <p class="text-italic">
              For genotype imputation using the TOPMed reference panel, refer to the 
              <Link to="https://imputation.biodatacatalyst.nhlbi.nih.gov/">TOPMed Imputation Server</Link>.
            </p>
              <div class="display-flex flex-align-center flex-justify-center">
                <IconBadge icon="database" tone="cool" size={5} class="margin-x-1" />
                <Link to={`/about/studies/topmed`}>See a list of the TOPMed data available in BDC</Link>
              </div>

          </section>

          <section id="recover" class="border-top-1px border-base-light margin-top-6">
            <h2>RECOVER</h2>
            <p>
              <Link to="https://recovercovid.org/">Researching COVID to Enhance Recovery (RECOVER)</Link>
              {' '}
              is a first-of-its-kind, patient-centered research initiative to understand,
              diagnose, and treat Long COVID. RECOVER research includes observational
              cohort studies, electronic health records analyses, pathobiology studies,
              tissue pathology studies, and clinical trials.
            </p>
            <p>
              RECOVER studies involve thousands of people from all walks of life, hundreds of research investigators, and millions of electronic health records (EHRs). RECOVER aims to achieve the following:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Understand the range of symptoms and impacts on quality of life for individuals experiencing Long COVID.  
              </li>
              <li>
                Define risk factors and causes associated with Long COVID.  
              </li>
              <li>
                Study how Long COVID changes over time and how those changes may relate to other illnesses.  
              </li>
              <li>
                Identify possible treatments for Long COVID symptoms.
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              The Data References and Access Information section on the RECOVER
              {' '}
              <Link to="https://recovercovid.org/data">Data</Link>
              {' '}
              page provides access to key resources for working with RECOVER data.
              These resources include Data Dictionaries, Data Release Notes, and Data
              Use Agreements for Adult/Pregnancy, Pediatric, and Tissue Pathology
              datasets. There are also additional Data Access Resources that support
              data access requests, data sharing compliance, and use of RECOVER datasets.
            </p>
            <div class="display-flex flex-align-center flex-justify-center">
              <IconBadge icon="database" tone="cool" size={5} class="margin-x-1" />
              <Link to={`/about/studies/recover`}>See a list of the RECOVER data available in BDC</Link>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="heartshare" class="border-top-1px border-base-light margin-top-6">
            <h2>HeartShare</h2>
            <p>
              <Link to="https://amphf.org/">HeartShare</Link>
              {' '}
              is an NHLBI-funded program to conduct large-scale analysis of phenotypic
              data, images, and omics from patients with heart failure with preserved
              ejection fraction (HFpEF) and controls to characterize disease mechanisms
              and identify therapeutic targets.
            </p>
            <p>
              HeartShare is comprised of retrospective and prospective components.
              HeartShare aggregates and harmonizes data from previously completed cohort
              studies and trials, including images and omics. Prospective data are
              generated from the HeartShare registry of up to 10,000 participants and
              deep phenotyping study cohorts involving up to 1,000 participants. Both
              cohorts will have baseline and longitudinal data.
            </p>
            <div class="display-flex flex-align-center flex-justify-center">
              <IconBadge icon="database" tone="cool" size={5} class="margin-x-1" />
              <Link to={`/about/studies/heartshare`}>See a list of the HeartShare data available in BDC</Link>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="nsrr" class="border-top-1px border-base-light margin-top-6">
            <h2>National Sleep Research Resource (NSRR)</h2>
            <p>
              <Link to="https://sleepdata.org/">National Sleep Research Resource (NSRR)</Link>
              {' '}
              brings polysomnography, actigraphy, questionnaire, and other sleep data
              from cohorts and clinical trials to BDC for secondary research in sleep
              and circadian science. BDC is working with NSRR to expand support for
              sleep data and analysis tools, improve sleep metadata and data models,
              and develop AI-assisted approaches to data harmonization.
            </p>
            <p>
              The NSRR encourages active engagement by the sleep and circadian
              communities, aiming to expand the breadth and depth of the sleep-related
              data and understand optimal methods of sleep data analysis.
            </p>
            <div class="display-flex flex-align-center flex-justify-center">
              <IconBadge icon="database" tone="cool" size={5} class="margin-x-1" />
              <Link to={`/about/studies/nsrr`}>See a list of the NSRR data available in BDC</Link>
            </div>
          </section>
          <section id="rmip" class="border-top-1px border-base-light margin-top-6">
            <h2>Regenerative Medicine Innovation Project (RMIP)</h2>
            <p>
              BDC is supporting the development of a centralized research resource for
              {' '}
              <Link to="https://www.nih.gov/regenerative-medicine-innovation-project-rmip">
                Regenerative Medicine Innovation Project (RMIP)
              </Link>
              {' '}
              data, with standardized data aggregation and processing across multiple
              data-generation sites. BDC also supports study registration and data
              ingest, helping make these data available for future research and reuse.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>

        <NextStepsAlert
          heading="Want to propose a new research community collaboration?"
        >
          <p class="usa-prose">
            Research programs interested in collaborating with BDC can express
            their interest with our Contact form.
          </p>

          <Link to="/help/contact-and-support">
            Propose New Research Community Collaboration
          </Link>
        </NextStepsAlert>
      </InPageNav>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
